[95.393044, "i", "cat > /home/github/build/failed/failed_reasons.txt << 'EOF'\nBUILD FAILURE ANALYSIS\n======================\n\nRepository: AgentOps-AI/agentops\nBuild Log: 24579293289-orig.log\n\nFailed Test:\n- tests/test_events.py::TestEvents::test_record_timestamp\n\nError Description:\n- The test creates an ActionEvent, waits 0.15 seconds, then records it\n- It expects event.init_timestamp != event.end_timestamp\n- Both timestamps show the same value: '2024-05-04T02:36:17.528Z'\n\nRoot Cause:\n- The get_ISO_time() function in agentops/helpers.py uses timespec='milliseconds'\n- This provides only millisecond precision (3 decimal places)\n- When timestamps are generated within the same millisecond or round to the same value,\n  they appear identical even after a 150ms delay\n- The record() method in client.py updates end_timestamp only if init_timestamp == end_timestamp,\n  but this comparison can fail due to insufficient precision\n\nSolution:\n- Change timestamp precision from 'milliseconds' to 'microseconds' in get_ISO_time()\n- This will provi"]
[95.3932, "i", "de 6 decimal places instead of 3, ensuring timestamps differ even for\n  sub-millisecond intervals\n\nFile to Fix:\n- agentops/helpers.py - line 30: change timespec='milliseconds' to timespec='microseconds'\nEOF\n"]
